thank you for  talking to me about what seems like it  was probably a very fun character to get  to explore  yeah oh she was a blast i'm curious when  the opportunity to play  one of these nine perfect strangers came  your way what was it that got you most  interested about the project since there  are  so many interesting so many things  there's so many things i got excited  about  um probably selfishly was that it was  filming in australia and  you know in this pandemic it's so hard  to get in and out of that country and  um i jumped at the opportunity to be  able to go there and  um see my family and friends over there  because  it's kind of impossible now yeah i mean  while you were shooting this did it sort  of feel like you were in your own little  world  totally it was really surreal it  kind of feels like a dream now because  it was like a year and a bit ago  um you know we were in this  like in paradise in the middle of it  felt really strange it was like we  what if i this doesn't we should be in  lockdown but  um you know australia did such a great  job of containing  everything that everything was open and  we could hang out and  you know we were by the beach and we  would just either be at this wellness  retreat or we'd be  in a waterfall or something it was it  was ridiculous  how involved was the process of creating  the look for your character how and how  much did that help you in finding who  she was  so much i mean the hair makeup  department and the wardrobe department  as well did  the real heavy lifting you know um we  would email back and forth about  different looks we wanted and  different outfits and um the yeah  when we did the makeup test  um that was when i really felt  uh jessica sort of come to life  ethan  there's some wild stuff that happens in  this show  and um one of those things is  and obviously i'll save it till after  it's a spoiler but it's having your nose  fall off  what was that like to do it was  i was so nervous because i think it was  like the  second or third scene i had done with  nicole  and i was like i guess i'm just gonna  have to go  for it and then she's gonna come in  um but they didn't use any uh makeup  which is cool they just had like cgi so  they just had dots on my face and then  this like funny prop  just my nose um i was practicing at home  in the mirror  well with my with my partner of like  okay is this a funny scream like should  i drop it like this  should i you know how would i what's the  truth behind this  um it was really fun i would also  imagine that you  could never have pictured yourself in a  delivery scene with  luke evans delivering bobby cannavale's  baby  so what goes to your head when you're in  a moment like that  just trying not to laugh they committed  to it  because that's what made it so funny and  so weird  and it just made me laugh and i just had  to buy my tongue  one of the sequences that i most enjoyed  was the potato sack race because  everybody actually seems to be having so  much fun in it  what was that like to shoot and how long  did you have to spend doing that  if i remember correctly i think we did  it in a day or maybe two  days mixed with some other scenes but it  was so fun i mean the sun was out and  beautiful green grass and we were all  just getting really into it i loved when  um  they used a slo-mo camera and we could  re-watch everyone's slo-mo face it was  that was fun if you're gonna get screwed  around with by anyone it seems like  nicole kidman  is a good choice to be doing that to you  so  what did you most enjoy about exploring  that dynamic between your characters and  having someone like her  as a scene partner especially with some  of the craziness that goes on  yeah i mean she's such a generous actor  she really gives you space to play  and find the scene and um  she's so patient it was amazing um  yeah she's she's just a wonderful and  you know she was a producer and so she  was a fabulous leader as well her and  melissa you know and all the women who  were producing this i mean bruno and  molly and  uh it was awesome what was your reaction  to the ending of the series learning  where things would  be left and how your character would end  up  yeah we actually didn't get the final um  episode script until like i think three  months into shooting or maybe longer  and it was really cool to like read  where your character is going to end up  in real time we'd kind of heard rumors  and we were wondering about it like  melvin and i would talk about  i wonder where ben and jessica end up  and is it going to be like the book or  is it going to be different and  it was awesome what was the most  challenging part of this shoot was there  a scene or a moment that was most  difficult because you do also have a lot  of emotional levels that you go through  yeah i mean honestly the most  challenging part i think was like  the amount of fake tans i'd have to go  and get getting my nails really done and  like getting my hair redone  i just cannot i have such admiration for  women who  do that on a weekly basis i do not have  the patience for it so  that was that was the most those nails  they were like  three inches long trying to do stuff  that's really hard  it's very impressive anybody that can  pull off the nails just in everyday life  lava what was it like to see yourself  with the tan  i mean especially the first time because  it seems like it's  you know it's quite noticeable yeah i  mean  if i stay in the sun long enough i can  get pretty dark i just i'm too lazy to  like lie out and you know in australia  there's such um  you know uh you can get like skin cancer  really easily so i've  been told to stay out of the sun but uh  it was um it was interesting i mean my  partner jimmy was i think more  surprised than i was  what was it like i mean you are one of  the characters that goes into this  as a couple so what was it like actually  having somebody  by your side to go through this with and  to have that  dynamic to explore yeah it was really it  was really interesting and i love  melvin you know we would get together  beforehand and sort of talk about these  scenes because the scenes were  really nuts and crazy and it was hard to  keep track of where our characters were  at each  time so it was really good to be able to  just have someone to whisper like okay  where are we in this one okay we've just  had  okay so we're here you know um  yeah it was good to have you know like a  a partner through it all and being able  to  explore not just what jessica's going  through but what jessica and ben are  going through as a couple as well  well i appreciate you talking to me  about it i had so much fun with your  character and getting to see you in a  row like this  so thank you

